> A deliberately messy file: every line below is legal AgentMark in a non-canonical shape.
> It exercises each rule of the formatter.

# Program: billing-desk
Chases unpaid invoices and imports invoice files.

Runs from the command line and as a service.

- start: [import-csv](#command-import-csv)

# Uses
- [constants](../constants.agent.md)
- [invoice](./records/invoice.agent.md)
- [every rule](./rules/*.agent.md)
- [billing rules](./billing/) as billing

# Import: crate reqwest as http_client
# Import: crate serde_json

# Record: Invoice
The thing we send out.

- customer: text
- amount
- due_date: date
- score: maybe int
- lines: list of text
> trailing note about the record, kept in place

# Rule: overdue Invoice
Unpaid and more than two weeks late.

- when: today > due + 14 days and status != "paid"

# Constant: fee
- value: 12.50 EUR

# Function: net_amount
The net amount without VAT.

- in: invoice: Invoice, vat: int = 19
- out: money
- touches: nothing
- steps:
  1. return (invoice.amount - invoice.amount * vat / 100) * 1

# Function: totals
Adds up what was sold in each region.

- in: sales
- out: region totals
- steps:
  1. group sales by region into by_region
  2. empty list of RegionTotal into totals
  3. for each region, region_sales in by_region:
     1. add RegionTotal to totals:
        - region
        - orders: count of region_sales
     2. add RegionTotal to totals:
        - region
        - orders: count of region_sales
  4. if count of totals > 0:
     1. print: "some"
     else:
     1. print: "none"
  5. return sort totals by revenue descending

# Function: fetch_all
- in: urls: list of text
- touches: AI, crm
- steps:
  1. try http get "https://api.example.com/rates" into rates
     otherwise:
     > fall back to the cache
     1. stop
  2. match rates:
     - ok v:
       1. print: "{v}"
     - error:
       1. stop
  3. parallel:
     1. do fetch_rates into rates
     2. do net_amount(invoice, 19) into n
  4. guard: not (reminder is empty or reminder length > 800) else stop

# Agent: chaser
Chases unpaid invoices.

- model: claude:haiku
- tools: email, crm, log
- memory: file
- timeout: 1 minute
> trailing property note

## Every Monday at 08:00
Looks at every invoice.

1. for each overdue invoice in crm.invoices:
   1. if invoice.score is some s:
      1. log: "Score {s}"
      else:
      > nothing to do for unscored invoices
      1. stop
   2. ask model with invoice: "Write a reminder for {invoice.customer}. Say \"thanks\" and use \{braces}." as Reminder into reminder
   3. email send customer: "{reminder}"
   4. crm update invoice: status = "reminded", score = 1

## On start
1. count of overdue invoices in crm.invoices into total
2. first i in state.invoices where i.id = id into found
3. log: "started"
4. print: "Done {total} {(total + 1) * 2}"

## Every 30 minutes
1. log: "tick"
> a note that sits at the very end of the block

## Do remind
1. log: "remind"

# Service: api
Serves invoices.

- listen: 0.0.0.0:8080
- state: AppState

## GET /invoices/{id}
1. respond 200 found
2. respond 404

# Command: import-csv
Reads an invoice file.

- in: path: text, dry_run: bool = false
- steps:
  1. read file path as list of Invoice into rows
  2. print: "n"

## Rust: fingerprint -> text
Hashes an invoice.

- in: invoice: Invoice
- touches: nothing

```rust
use sha2::{Digest, Sha256};

    format!("{:x}", Sha256::digest(invoice.id.as_bytes()))
```

# Binding: pdf
Renders documents.

- crate: printpdf
- effect: unverified
- proposed-effect: network

## render(doc: Document) -> bytes
Draws a document.

  ```rust
  Ok(vec![])
  ```

